sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2022-tame-28> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Mutations in electrogenic genes can produce coordinated, long-range anatomical change" ;
    dct:description "Because the same membrane-voltage dynamics can be produced by many ion-channel combinations and bioelectric states act across tissue distances, evolution can swap channels freely, and simple mutations in electrogenic genes can cause long-range, highly coordinated changes in anatomy (supported by KCNH8 and a connexin in an evolutionary shift of fish fin morphology)." ;
    delphi:context "Levin M, “Technological Approach to Mind Everywhere: An Experimentally-Grounded Framework for Understanding Diverse Bodies and Minds”, Frontiers in systems neuroscience (2022), doi:10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201; section “Evolutionary Aspects › Somatic Bioelectrics Reveals the Origin of Complex Cognitive Systems”. Scope: Animal morphological evolution, e.g. fish fins" ;
    dct:type "historical-inference" .
}

